    task: "Write a for-and-against essay (220–270 words) on the following topic: Buying local: good or bad?",
    taskAr: "اكتب مقالة تعرض فيها حجج المؤيدين والمعارضين لشراء المنتجات المحلية (من مزارع ومحلات وورش قريبة) بدلاً من المنتجات المستوردة، ثم اختم بحكمك المتوازن.",
    words: [220, 270],
    model: [
      "It is often argued that shoppers should buy local products, such as vegetables from nearby farms or furniture from neighbourhood workshops, rather than imported goods. Not everyone agrees, however. This essay will consider the arguments on both sides before reaching a balanced conclusion.",
      "The main rationale for buying local is that it supports the community. Money spent in a nearby shop is more likely to stay in the area, which helps to create jobs and keep small family businesses alive. A further point in favour is freshness: fruit and vegetables picked close to home need less storage and transport, so they usually taste better. Moreover, shorter journeys are widely believed to reduce pollution.",
      "On the other hand, critics point to several drawbacks. The most obvious downside is cost, since small producers cannot always match the low prices of large companies. Although local goods are often fresher, the choice may be limited, and some products simply cannot be grown or made nearby. Admittedly, a local label is attractive, but the notion that local is automatically better can be a pitfall: a product may be made nearby and still harm the environment if the methods used are wasteful.",
      "In conclusion, buying local brings clear benefits to communities and, in many cases, to quality. Nevertheless, higher prices and limited variety cannot be ignored. Despite these drawbacks, I believe on balance that the advantages outweigh the disadvantages, provided that shoppers compare prices and choose carefully."
    ],
